## 12. Risk register

| Risk | Mitigation |
| --- | --- |
| Inline DB schema grows too large | Create real `0002_web_product.sql`, then incrementally move migrations out of `db/state.rs`. |
| Markdown XSS | Server-side sanitation, strict tests, no client-rendered unsanitized HTML. |
| Large diffs freeze browser | Server pagination and client virtualization. |
| WebSocket drops lose events | Persist `web_activity_events` and replay by sequence. |
| Permissions drift from UI | Server-side RBAC and capability checks on every mutation. |
| Existing webhook engine state type conflicts with web router | Use `WebState` and nested routers; avoid changing webhook handler signatures. |
| Git operations block async runtime | Use `spawn_blocking` around heavy `git2` tree/diff operations. |
| GitLab/Jeryu source-of-truth ambiguity | Define JeRyu web tables as UI/product metadata; Git refs/blobs remain Git source of truth; CI/release remains existing JeRyu/GitLab subsystems. |

